# Shell scripts must stay LF. The agent hook templates under
# apps/desktop/src/main/lib/agent-setup/templates/*.sh are read VERBATIM and
# written out as the runtime hook scripts (see notify-hook.ts); a CRLF here
# would put a \r in the shebang/commands and break bash on Windows — defeating
# the (HOOK-FORK-DIET) reliability work. core.autocrlf=true must not touch them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Lingui rewrites every catalog with LF. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows
# checkout hands it CRLF instead, so each regeneration rewrites all 34 files
# and leaves them stat-dirty — which made (I18N-CATALOG-GATE) report drift on
# a tree whose content was identical. Pinning the catalogs to LF makes
# "regenerate, then diff" mean the same thing on a maintainer's machine and
# on the runner.
packages/i18n/locales/**/messages.po text eol=lf
packages/i18n/locales/**/messages.ts text eol=lf
